@startuml 02-containers

!pragma layout smetana lefttoright

title FlowAI Platform - Task flow (runtime slice)

package "Automation layer" {
    [Webhook Handler] as wh
    [Jira Poller] as jira
    [GitLab Handler] as gl
}

package "Queue + operator graph" {
    [Router] as router
    database "Router DB" as routerDb
}

package "Operator-facing (UI/GW/State Registry/Secret Registry independent)" {
    [API Gateway] as gw
    [State Registry] as stateRegistry
    database "State Registry DB" as stateRegistryDb
    database "Secret Registry" as secretRegistry
}

package "Executor fleet (multi-cluster)" {
    [Executor A (k8s-A)] as exA
    [Executor B (k8s-B)] as exB
    [Executor local (Docker)] as exL
}

' --- Automation -> Router (publish to incoming queue) ---
wh --> router : REST publish task
jira --> router : REST publish task
gl --> router : REST publish task

' --- Router internals ---
router --> routerDb : persist queue + executor pool state
note right of router
  Main purpose: organize task queue.
  Owns: incoming list, executor wait list,
  executor pool (registry, capacity, slots_in_use),
  task assignment state.
  Receives: Auto submissions, EX registration,
  EX ready signals, EX status updates, EX pulls.
end note

' --- EX -> Router (executor fleet talks to queue manager) ---
exA --> router : REST register, signal ready, pull next, post status
exB --> router : REST register, signal ready, pull next, post status
exL --> router : REST register, signal ready, pull next, post status

' --- EX -> State Registry (historical event writes) ---
exA --> stateRegistry : REST POST /events (historical)
exB --> stateRegistry : REST POST /events (historical)
exL --> stateRegistry : REST POST /events (historical)
exA --> stateRegistry : REST GET control requests
exB --> stateRegistry : REST GET control requests
exL --> stateRegistry : REST GET control requests

stateRegistry --> stateRegistryDb : read/write historical state

' --- EX -> Secret Registry (open env at task start) ---
exA --> secretRegistry : REST open env
exB --> secretRegistry : REST open env
exL --> secretRegistry : REST open env

' --- Operator graph: UI (not shown here), GW, State Registry, Secret Registry ---
' GW talks to State Registry and Secret Registry independently. No Router connection in this graph.

note right of gw
  Auth-aware reverse proxy.
  Routes UI requests to State Registry or Secret Registry.
  NO connection to Router.
end note

note right of stateRegistry
  State Registry.
  NO connection to Router.
  Receives historical events
  from executors and
  queries/control requests from GW.
  Executors read pending
  control requests from here.
end note

note right of secretRegistry
  Secret Registry.
  NO connection to Router or State Registry.
  Receives open env
  from executors and
  store calls from GW.
end note

note right
  Router is the queue manager between producers, executors, and services.
  Auto publishes to Router.
  Services consume from Router.
  Executors pull from Router wait list.
  UI does NOT touch Router. UI -> GW -> State Registry (read), GW -> Secret Registry (secret CRUD).
end note

@enduml
